Subject: [PATCH] feat: add pre-tool input transformers
X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: generic pre-tool transformer hook/config/docs
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: upstream-candidate
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none

Patch intent:
Transform configured tool JSON before pre_tool policy evaluation.

Why it exists:
Lets local adapters normalize or rewrite tool input without changing policy-gate
semantics; non-goal is replacing or bypassing the gate.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/mod.rs calls hooks::transform_tool_input from
Registry tool execution before hooks::run_pre_tool_gate;
crates/jcode-base/src/hooks.rs owns command execution, timeout, JSON
replacement, and fail-open behavior; crates/jcode-base/src/config.rs,
config/default_file.rs, config/env_overrides.rs,
crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs, and docs/HOOKS.md wire pre_tool_transform
and its timeout. External RTK plugin catalog content consumes this hook and its
configured plugin path.

Update guidance:
When upstream moves Registry execution or hook configuration, preserve
transform-before-gate ordering, pass transformed JSON to the gate, retain
original input on invalid output, nonzero exit, spawn failure, empty output, or
timeout, and keep existing gate timeout/failure behavior.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-base tool_transformer
